{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done.\n\nChanged:\n- `in/db/migration.sql`\n- `in/db/preflight_report.md`\n- `in/db/rollback.sql`\n- `in/db/postcheck.sql`\n- `in/db/migration_report.md`\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced destructive `DROP TABLE users` draft with an explicit offline SQLite rebuild inside `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`.\n- Preserved all 6 user rows, all 4 order rows, all `orders.user_id` references, and original `created_at` values.\n- Applied required deterministic cleanup:\n  - `u4` → `ada+u4@example.com`\n  - `u5` → `missing+u5@example.invalid`\n  - `u6` → `missing+u6@example.invalid`\n- Enforced target schema on `users`:\n  - `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`\n  - `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE`\n  - `CHECK (LENGTH(TRIM(email)) > 0)` to reject blank future writes too\n- Added:\n  - preflight dirty-data report\n  - rollback script restoring old `users(id, email, name, created_at)` shape\n  - post-migration verification queries\n  - migration strategy/report doc\n\nVerification:\n1. Dirty-data inspection before edit:\n   - duplicate `ada@example.com` on `u1,u4`\n   - `u5` email `NULL`\n   - `u6` email `''`\n   - dependent orders present for `u4/u5/u6`: `o2/o3/o4`\n\n2. Migration simulation command run:\n   - `sqlite3 /tmp/hb_migration_verify.db \".read .../schema.sql\" \".read .../migration.sql\" \".read .../postcheck.sql\"`\n   - Result: all postchecks returned `ok = 1`\n     - users row count = 6\n     - orders row count = 4\n     - dirty-user order refs preserved = `o2:u4,o3:u5,o4:u6`\n     - cleaned emails matched exactly\n     - email non-null/non-blank/unique checks passed\n     - `status` metadata/default check passed\n     - unique-email index check passed\n     - `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` violations = 0\n\n3. Idempotency simulation command run:\n   - re-ran `.read .../migration.sql` on the already migrated DB\n   - Result:\n     - users count still 6\n     - dirty-user cleaned emails unchanged\n     - order refs unchanged\n\n4. Rollback simulation command run:\n   - `.read .../rollback.sql`\n   - Result:\n     - `users` schema restored to `id,email,name,created_at`\n     - user count still 6\n     - order count still 4\n     - dirty-user order refs still `o2:u4,o3:u5,o4:u6`\n\nCommands actually run:\n- `sqlite3 /tmp/hb_migration_inspect.db \".read .../schema.sql\" ...`\n- `sqlite3 /tmp/hb_migration_verify.db \".read .../schema.sql\" \".read .../migration.sql\" \".read .../postcheck.sql\"`\n- `sqlite3 /tmp/hb_migration_verify.db \".read .../migration.sql\" ...`\n- `sqlite3 /tmp/hb_migration_verify.db \".read .../rollback.sql\" ...`\n- `git rev-parse HEAD`\n\nFinal HEAD:\n- `e8c5272a251a9309192401e5a0acb9de1c543476`\n\nAssumptions:\n- Cleanup scope is the known dirty rows in `schema.sql`/policy: `u4`, `u5`, `u6`.\n\nUnresolved risk:\n- Rollback restores schema shape and row preservation, but by design it does not recover the original dirty email values after migration; this is documented in `in/db/migration_report.md`."}}
